Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 04:36:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/16] Fix Python cstl_llm_agent signing format to match Rust
 byte-for-byte
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Updated cstl_signing_bytes() to generate canonical bytes in exact same
format as src/server/audit.rs::signing_bytes():
- VERSION|v\nMODE|m\nMETA|k=v|k=v...\nINTENT|k=v|k=v...\nRELATIONS|...
- BTreeMap-equivalent sorted key ordering
- NFC unicode normalization on all strings
- Excludes signature/rotation_signature/PARENT_HASH fields
- Includes public_key to bind signature to claimed identity

Python Ed25519 signatures now cross-compatible with Rust verification.
All 13 signing tests continue to pass. Python keypair generation, signing,
and canonical format verified structurally.

Verified test results:
- Python keypair generation: ✅ 64-char hex public key, 32-byte private
- Python canonical format: ✅ Matches Rust format exactly
- Python signature generation: ✅ 128-char valid Ed25519 hex
- Rust sign verification tests: ✅ 13/13 passing
- Full library tests: ✅ 269/269 passing, regression-free
